## Variable with different types in the alternatives

```catala
declaration enumeration E:
  -- A content integer
  -- B content money

declaration scope S:
  context e content E
  output o content boolean

scope S:
  definition e equals A content 1
  definition o equals match e with pattern
    -- A content x or B content x: x = x
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope S
┌─[ERROR]─
│
│  The variable x has type money in pattern B but type integer in pattern A.
│
├─➤ tests/enum/bad/or_pattern_type_mismatch.catala_en:15.33-34:
│    │
│ 15 │     -- A content x or B content x: x = x
│    │                                 ‾
├─ Variable with different types in the alternatives
│
├─➤ tests/enum/bad/or_pattern_type_mismatch.catala_en:15.18-19:
│    │
│ 15 │     -- A content x or B content x: x = x
│    │                  ‾
└─ Variable with different types in the alternatives
#return code 123#
```
